-- title:
--   Free corner datum on H¹(Γ₀(N)∩Γ₁(r),𝒪) with Σ-pin
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k$, let $p\neq 2$ be a prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$ (a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ with an action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ factoring through a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$) which is absolutely irreducible, for which no subspace of any scalar extension is stable under an index-two subgroup of the Galois group unless it is $\bot$ or $\top$ (hypothesis `hTW`), and which is ordinary at $p$ in the sense that above every place over $p$ there is a free rank-one line, stable under the decomposition group, modulo which inertia acts trivially. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, and $N$ a nonzero level with $p\nmid N$ and all prime factors in $S$. Let $\mathrm{Smin}\subseteq S$ contain $p$ and satisfy: for primes $q\neq p$, $q\in\mathrm{Smin}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$; each $q\in\mathrm{Smin}$, $q\neq p$, divides $N$ and has unipotent inertia at $q$ (characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ on inertia); each prime $q\neq p$ outside $\mathrm{Smin}$ dividing $N$ satisfies $q^2\mid N$; and no prime $q\neq p$ satisfies $q^3\mid N$. Let $r\geq 5$ be a prime with $r\notin S$, $r\nmid Np$, $p\nmid r-1$, and $(\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_r))^2\neq (r+1)^2$ for every Frobenius element at every place over $r$. Assume $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ is spanned over $\mathbb C$ by the $\mathbb Z$-lattice of forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients. Let $\theta_0$ be a ring homomorphism from the anemic Hecke algebra `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$ with $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$) to $k$ such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ and every Frobenius at $\ell$ the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho$ is $X^2-\theta_0(T_\ell)X+\ell$, and let $\pi_{T_0}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map from the localisation $\mathbb T_0=$ `heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ₀` to $\mathcal O$. Then there exist: the subgroup $H_0\leq(\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$ characterised as the kernel of reduction to $\mathbb Z/r$ (so that $\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr)=\Gamma_0(N)\cap\Gamma_1(r)$), a level comparison $h_{10}:\$`LevelLE (N*r) (N*r) ⊤ H₀ 1`, a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra $\mathbb T^{(0)}$ acting $\mathcal O$-compatibly on $H^1=$ `H1 (N*r) H₀ 𝒪` (additive homomorphisms from $\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr)$ to $\mathcal O$), a corner datum $cd_0$ on this action (an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb T^{(0)}$, an index, and a level pairing on the resulting corner ring and corner submodule), an $\mathcal O$-algebra isomorphism $e_0$ from the corner ring onto $\mathbb T_0$, with corner module finite and free over $\mathcal O$, an element $t_p$ of the corner ring, and families $t_{\mathrm{full}},c_{\mathrm{full}}$ indexed by the generator type `Gen (N*r) S` with values in $\mathbb T^{(0)}$ and $\mathcal O$, together with a proof $h_{W_0}$ that the corner submodule lies inside the image, under the degeneracy map `iDegL`, of the parabolic homomorphisms on $\Gamma_0(Nr)$, such that: (i) for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid Nr$, the element $e_0^{-1}$ of the image of $T_\ell$ in $\mathbb T_0$ acts on the corner module as `heckeT` at $\ell$; (ii) $t_p$ is a unit and acts both as `heckeT` and as `heckeTlower` at $p$; (iii) the submodule of the corner module killed by the kernel of $\pi_{T_0}\circ e_0$ is nonzero, and the $\mathcal O$-rank of the corner module is the product of its rank with the $\mathcal O$-rank of the corner ring; (iv) every element of $\mathbb T^{(0)}$ acts on $H^1$ through the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by the operator family `opFamily` (Hecke and diamond operators indexed by `Gen`); (v) for every generator $g$ which, if of the form $U_q$, has $q\mid N$, the operator $t_{\mathrm{full}}(g)$ acts as `opFamily` at $g$, and $t_{\mathrm{full}}(g)-c_{\mathrm{full}}(g)$ lies in the maximal ideal of the splitting at the chosen index; (vi) any $v\in H^1$ which, for all such $g$ and all $k$, satisfies $(t_{\mathrm{full}}(g)-c_{\mathrm{full}}(g))^n v\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}^k H^1$ for some $n$, lies in the corner submodule; (vii) for primes $q\mid N$ with $q\neq p$ and $q^2\mid N$, $c_{\mathrm{full}}(U_q)\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$; (viii) the corner ring acts faithfully on the corner module; (ix) the diamond operators `diamondRaw` for $\Gamma_0(Nr)$ act trivially on the corner submodule; (x) there is a prime $\ell_0\nmid Nrp$ such that for every uniformiser $\varpi$, any corner element $v$ with $T_{\ell_0}v-(\ell_0+1)v\in\varpi H^1$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in the corner module; (xi) the pairing of $cd_0$ agrees with [`CuspForm.Bfam 𝒪 (N*r) H₀ h₁₀`](def/CuspForm_CornerPairingFamily.html#L57) on the corner module via $h_{W_0}$; and (xii) the corner module is free over the corner ring.
--
--   This is the lower package of the level-raising step at the residue characteristic: it produces, at the auxiliary level $\Gamma_0(N)\cap\Gamma_1(r)$ with $p\nmid N$, a corner of the cohomology whose corner ring is the localised anemic Hecke algebra $\mathbb T_0$ and whose corner module is free over it, together with the $\Sigma$-normalisation $U_q\equiv 0 \pmod{\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}}$ at primes $q$ with $q^2\mid N$. Its conjuncts form the input block for the relative Taylor–Wiles rung, and it is cited by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_ordinaryCondition_of_finiteAt_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_ordinaryCondition_of_finiteAt_of_not_cube_dvd).
